@* First-time visitor, no saved theme (ViewData["EinvTheme"] null — the layout sets it from
   ThemePreference.Read): follow the OS/browser setting. Render as the very first thing in <head>; it
   runs synchronously so the attribute lands before anything paints (no flash of the wrong theme).
   With a saved theme the layout renders data-bs-theme server-side and this outputs nothing.
   (ViewData, not a model: a null partial model would fall back to the page's model.) *@
@if (ViewData["EinvTheme"] is not string)
{
    <script>
        (function () {
            var dark = window.matchMedia && window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)").matches;
            document.documentElement.setAttribute("data-bs-theme", dark ? "dark" : "light");
        })();
    </script>
}
